        "original_id": "2cd16d69-435e-5f12-b71e-c477d4fc2bf0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Thésée, Ovid's Metamorphoses\n- People: Jean-Baptiste Lully, Philippe Quinault, Louis XIV\n- Genres: tragédie en musique, tragédie lyrique, French opera\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully was born Giovanni Battista Lulli on 28 November 1632 and later became an Italian-born French composer, instrumentalist, and dancer.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully spent most of his life working at the court of Louis XIV of France.\n- Tragédie en musique, also called tragédie lyrique, is a genre of French opera introduced by Jean-Baptiste Lully.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully's followers used tragédie en musique until the second half of the eighteenth century.\n- Thésée is a tragédie en musique, an early type of French opera, structured as a prologue and five acts.\n- Thésée has music by Jean-Baptiste Lully and a libretto by Philippe Quinault.\n- Thésée is based on Ovid's Metamorphoses.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully died on 22 March 1687.",
